STRUCTURE=CONSTRAINT under-determined: a valid color+eligibility+degree-preserving 2-swap EXISTS at n=5,6
  => the parity/eligibility/degree constraints are NECESSARY but NOT SUFFICIENT to pin the metagraph;
     they are its 'parity skeleton'; the tournament-iso structure selects the actual realization.
PARITY THEOREM REDUCTION: sigma (complement-fold) PRESERVES merged nodes; node = union of sigma-orbits
  (fixed=grid-sym, else pairs); tiling_count = #gridsym + 2*#pairs => parity = #gridsym mod 2.
  SC node has ODD #gridsym (crux, verified), NS has 0 => SC odd / NS even tiling count.
IDENTITY: #grid-sym tilings = 2^floor((n-1)^2/4) = 2^(half-tiling quarter-square size); blue lines = half.
